---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Ladder from '../components/Ladder.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const strengths = (await getCollection('strengths')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
---

<Layout
  title="How I work | COM<tech> Consulting"
  description="Three ways to work with Anders Hybertz: an independent outside view, hands-on software architecture, or leading the technical delivery. Architecture, cloud and AI, technical leadership, IT advisory, and software auditing."
  closeHeading="Not sure which fits yet?"
  closeBody="Start with the problem itself. A short description of the situation is enough for a first conversation."
>
  <div slot="opening" class="intro">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-title">How I work</h1>
      <p class="lead">Three ways to work together, from an outside view to leading the technical delivery. The work usually sits between architecture, delivery, and technical leadership.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section section-white" aria-labelledby="h-ways">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="h-ways" class="h2">Three ways to work together</h2>
        <p>Each way includes the services listed under it, and each has recent work behind it.</p>
      </div>
      <Ladder detailed />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-sit">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="h-sit" class="h2">When clients usually call</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="ruled">
        <div><h3>The system has become too hard to reason about</h3><p>Responsibilities are blurred, integrations have grown fragile, and every change feels more expensive than it should.</p></div>
        <div><h3>An important technical decision needs firmer footing</h3><p>Modernisation, cloud direction, architecture boundaries, or whether a proposed path is actually worth the cost.</p></div>
        <div><h3>The team needs senior technical direction</h3><p>Clearer judgement, better structure, and help carrying the work through delivery in a sustainable way.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-white" aria-labelledby="h-principles">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="h-principles" class="h2">Principles</h2>
        <p>What you can expect from the way I work, whichever of the three it is.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="principles">
        {strengths.map(s => (
          <li>
            <h3 class="h2-sm">{s.data.title}</h3>
            <p>{s.data.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .principles { list-style: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 40px 48px; }
  .principles h3 { margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 20px; }
  .principles p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .principles { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 28px; }
  }
</style>
